+// [ohos-fix] Whether the gelu ops may dispatch to oneDNN on this platform.
+// oneDNN's aarch64 eltwise gelu path does not terminate here: with USE_MKLDNN=ON a
+// plain at::gelu(float32, 100 elements) spins forever in the run-time generated
+// (xbyak_aarch64) kernel -- the process stays runnable and burns CPU -- while the
+// same call returns in milliseconds with oneDNN disabled at run time
+// (setUserEnabledMkldnn(false)) and in the pre-adaptation build (USE_MKLDNN=OFF).
+// The liveness probe of patch 0017 cannot gate this: mmap+mprotect succeed, the
+// generated kernel still loops. Other oneDNN ops on this build are unaffected
+// (relu / conv2d / linear / matmul / softmax complete normally), and neither the
+// oneDNN ISA cap (ASIMD/ASIMDHP/DEFAULT) nor OMP_NUM_THREADS changes the outcome,
+// so the workaround is scoped to gelu: it falls back to ATen's own vectorized and
+// scalar kernels, which keep the operator fully functional.
+#if defined(__OHOS__)
+constexpr bool gelu_oneDNN_usable_here() {
+  return false;
+}
+#else
+constexpr bool gelu_oneDNN_usable_here() {
+  return true;
+}
+#endif
 #endif
 
